 CODE
Art. 2.3.32.
Joint management 
Without prejudice to the provisions of Article 2.3.31, the consent of both spouses is required for:
1¡ acquire, alienate or encumber with real rights property subject to mortgage; 
2¡ acquire, assign or pledge businesses or operations of any kind; 
3¡ enter into, renew or terminate leases of more than nine years, grant commercial leases and farm leases; 
4¡ assign or pledge mortgage claims; 
5¡ to collect the price of the alienation of immovable property or the repayment of mortgage claims, and to discharge registrations; 
6¡ to accept or refuse a bequest or donation where it is stipulated that the property bequeathed or donated is to be held in common; 
7¡ to take out a loan; 
8¡ to take out consumer credit, unless such credit is necessary for the needs of the household or the education of children.
